From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 05:33:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] hjviewer: pin builds to the hjviewer server, WebSocket +
 WebRTC by default

HJV_SERVER and HJV_SERVER_KEY, read at build time, name the server every
build talks to; a build without them behaves as upstream. Such a build:

- locks the ID/relay server, API server and key to it, so the UI cannot
  point it elsewhere, and hides those settings;
- always uses WebSocket: wss://<server>/ws/id and /ws/relay on 443, the
  one port firewalls reliably let out (an https API server is what makes
  check_ws pick wss://);
- turns WebRTC on by default, which upstream only does for its public
  servers, so peers still connect directly when their networks allow it;
- turns off update checks and auto update, which follow upstream releases;
- is named HJViewer (kr.ac.yonsei.hjviewer on Android and iOS).

Hooked into load_custom_client, which every process runs before it reads
its config, and into the Flutter init path that skips it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
